<!--
  The bounded mutation set: what the app decides, not what it holds.

  Coverage says a line ran; mutation says a test would have noticed if the line
  were wrong. Both are needed, but mutation costs one test run per mutant, so
  the set is deliberately narrow — the files that make decisions (admission,
  activation, eligibility, pacing, engine composition, windowing, startup
  timing) and not the data classes, whose equality and JSON round-trips are
  already pinned by domain_equality_test.dart and would generate hundreds of
  trivial mutants.

  Widgets, goldens and the FFI wrappers are out: their oracle is a rendered
  frame or a platform channel, not an exit code.

  The command runs only the suites that reach these files, which is what keeps a
  mutant at ~8s instead of a 30s full suite. Run it against a throwaway git
  worktree — mutation_test rewrites sources in place, so a crash mid-run leaves
  a mutated file behind:

    git worktree add --detach /tmp/mutation HEAD
    cd /tmp/mutation/app && flutter pub get
    dart pub global activate mutation_test
    dart pub global run mutation_test ../tool/mutation/decision_logic.xml
-->
<mutations version="1.2">
  <files>
    <file>lib/core/domain/model_activation.dart</file>
    <file>lib/core/domain/model_admission.dart</file>
    <file>lib/core/domain/device_eligibility.dart</file>
    <file>lib/core/domain/download_pace.dart</file>
    <file>lib/core/domain/model_speed.dart</file>
    <file>lib/core/domain/response_style_mapping.dart</file>
    <file>lib/core/domain/model_profile_spec.dart</file>
